==Trivia==
*Warumongar's Japanese name (ワルモーン ''Warumōn'') is a portmanteau of 悪い ''warui'' (bad/evil) or 悪者 ''warumono'' (bad guy) and ''[[Dark Priest Mamon|Mamon]]''. It may also be a reference to [[wikia:twinbee:Dr. Warumon|Dr. Warumon]] from the ''[[wikipedia:TwinBee (series)|TwinBee]]'' series or the Kumamoto police mascot [https://www.asahi.com/sp/ajw/articles/16081918 Warumon].

